INT. OBSERVATORY BALLROOM - NIGHT

A gala under a brass telescope. Strings tune. Champagne flutes glint. Couples drift to the dance floor.

CELESTE MARCHETTI, 30s, stands alone by the window in a green gown. Her ex, JULIAN VOSS, 30s, enters in a tuxedo, hesitates, then crosses to her. A WAITER, 20s, passes with a tray. Behind them, ISOLDE FAIRWEATHER, 60s, Celeste's aunt, watches over her fan.

JULIAN
You came.

CELESTE
You invited me.

JULIAN
I didn't think you'd say yes.

ISOLDE
(calling over)
Celeste, darling, the cake!

CELESTE
In a minute, Auntie.

The waiter offers a flute. Julian takes two. Hands one to her.

WAITER
Compliments of the house.

JULIAN
To old times.

CELESTE
To new ones.

ISOLDE
(approaching)
Julian, you've gotten thin.

JULIAN
Hello, Isolde.

ISOLDE
Are you eating?

CELESTE
Auntie.

The music swells. Julian offers a hand. She looks at it. Behind her, Isolde fans faster. The waiter retreats.

JULIAN
One dance.

CELESTE
One.

She takes it. They step into the crowd, stiff at first, then not. Isolde lowers the fan and sighs. The waiter sets down his tray and leaves it.

ISOLDE
(to the waiter)
Fetch the cake knife, would you? She'll want it later.

WAITER
Ma'am?

ISOLDE
I said she'd want it. Go.
